From: Pablo Neira Ayuso <pablo@netfilter.org>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 10:18:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: conntrack: always lower timeout for non-closing
 RST packets
References: bsc#1258210
Patch-mainline: 6.18.61
Git-commit: 73df81b38cb7f70a347a97370386378a86e53019

commit 73df81b38cb7f70a347a97370386378a86e53019 upstream.

The existing check might extend the timeout if the ESTABLISHED timeout
has been tuned to be lower than UNACK via sysctl. Reported by sashiko.

Fixes: bf80e6802273 ("netfilter: conntrack: tcp: use UNACK timeout for non-closing RST packets")
Signed-off-by: Pablo Neira Ayuso <pablo@netfilter.org>
Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>
Signed-off-by: Robert Frohl <rfrohl@suse.com>
---
 net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_proto_tcp.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_proto_tcp.c b/net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_proto_tcp.c
index 456721e40ed0..03b32bd397d3 100644
--- a/net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_proto_tcp.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_proto_tcp.c
@@ -1326,7 +1326,8 @@ int nf_conntrack_tcp_packet(struct nf_conn *ct,
 	    timeouts[new_state] > timeouts[TCP_CONNTRACK_RETRANS])
 		timeout = timeouts[TCP_CONNTRACK_RETRANS];
 	else if (unlikely(index == TCP_RST_SET &&
-			  new_state == TCP_CONNTRACK_ESTABLISHED))
+			  new_state == TCP_CONNTRACK_ESTABLISHED) &&
+		 timeouts[new_state] > timeouts[TCP_CONNTRACK_UNACK])
 		timeout = timeouts[TCP_CONNTRACK_UNACK];
 	else if ((ct->proto.tcp.seen[0].flags | ct->proto.tcp.seen[1].flags) &
 		 IP_CT_TCP_FLAG_DATA_UNACKNOWLEDGED &&
-- 
2.56.0

